# ============================================================
# arest rebuild (merged 2026-07-20): carriers regenerate on demand;
# composed stations and oracle outputs are build ephemera.
# The journal files are NOT ephemera - they track.
# ============================================================
apps/*/design-state
apps/*/norma-answer
apps/*/oracle-report.txt
apps/*/verbalization-report.txt
apps/*/verbalization-report.html
apps/*/.combined/
apps/*/checker-answer

# the toolchain (tracked since 2026-07-20): only build ephemera stay out —
# composed stations and oracle outputs regenerate on demand. The journal
# files are NOT ephemera: they are the store of record, and they track.
bin/
obj/
*.class
# every composed .g.js, not two of them by name. Listing them individually is
# why 53 stray probes (dump*.g.js, probeA.g.js, cw.g.js, ...) accumulated here
# unignored: each new probe got a new name and nobody added it. A composed file
# is a byte-concatenation of head + canon + carriers + a tail, so it is always
# regenerable and never worth tracking.
tools/js-runner/*.g.js
# the stations wall's whole output tree (composed sources + per-station
# stdout it diffs), by DIRECTORY per the lesson above — never by name.
tools/wall/stations.out/
# the rust station's composed sources: compose.py's chunked projection of the
# canon and carriers. Same rule as every other composed file — a byte
# concatenation of head + canon + carriers is always regenerable and never
# worth tracking. By PATTERN, not by name.
tools/rust-station/src/*.g.rs
tools/web-runner/composed.page.g.js
tools/java-runner/Composed.g.java
tools/cs-runner/Composed.g.cs
tools/wpf-runner/Composed.g.cs
tools/ifactr-oracle/Composed.g.cs
tools/norma-oracle/design-state
tools/norma-oracle/norma-answer
# the provenance sidecars WriteCarrier stamps beside each carrier
# (Verifier.cs:4303) -- same class as the carrier they annotate.
tools/norma-oracle/*.source
tools/norma-oracle/*.metamodel
tools/norma-oracle/oracle-report.txt
tools/norma-oracle/verbalization-report.txt
tools/norma-oracle/verbalization-report.html
tools/wall/csprobe/Composed.g.cs
tools/wall/cont.g.js
tools/wall/cont[A-D].txt
tools/wall/journal.test

# generated procedural projections (transform_rust.py emits src/main.rs per app)
tools/rust-runner/src/main.rs
tools/rust-runner/Cargo.lock
derived-state
tools/wall/derive-store.g.js
tools/wall/derive-refresh.g.js

__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The JUnit console launcher: a test-only binary, fetched not vendored.
# tools/java-runner/fetch-junit.sh gets it; every other build output
# here (bin/, obj/, target/) is ignored for the same reason.
tools/lib/*.jar
